{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/python-attrs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/python-attrs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/python-attrs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/python-attrs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/python-attrs/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/python-attrs/attrs","description":"Python Classes Without Boilerplate","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/deployments","created_at":"2015-01-27T15:01:01Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T18:21:48Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-08T12:01:47Z","git_url":"git://github.com/python-attrs/attrs.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:python-attrs/attrs.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/python-attrs/attrs.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/python-attrs/attrs","homepage":"https://www.attrs.org/","size":4710,"stargazers_count":5680,"watchers_count":5680,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":410,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":139,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["attributes","boilerplate","classes","oop","python"],"visibility":"public","forks":410,"open_issues":139,"watchers":5680,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/pulls/238","html_url":"https://github.com/python-attrs/attrs/pull/238","diff_url":"https://github.com/python-attrs/attrs/pull/238.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/python-attrs/attrs/pull/238.patch","merged_at":"2018-07-12T10:19:24Z"},"body":"Here's a first take at PEP484-compatible pyi stubs.  The discussion in #215 has been mostly focused on runtime type checking, so I wanted to make sure that the plan discussed there will work with static analysis as well.\r\n\r\nHere's a quick test of the stubs that I put together to run against mypy:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom typing import cast\r\nimport attr\r\n\r\n@attr.s\r\nclass C(object):\r\n    x : int = attr.ib(convert=int)\r\n    y: str = attr.ib()\r\n\r\nc = C('1', 'foo')  # E: Too many arguments for \"C\"\r\nc.x = 2\r\nc.y = 'bar'\r\nc > C()  # E: Unsupported left operand type for > (\"C\")\r\nstr(c)\r\n\r\n# errors below are correctly detected:\r\nc.x = 'foo'  # E: Incompatible types in assignment (expression has type \"str\", variable has type \"int\")\r\nc.y = 1  # E: Incompatible types in assignment (expression has type \"int\", variable has type \"str\")\r\n\r\nD = attr.make_class('D', {'x': cast(attr._CountingAttr, attr.ib())})\r\nd = D(2)\r\n# errors below are not correctly detected (mypy knows nothing about D other than that it's a type)\r\nd.x ='foo'\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nmypy knows nothing about the dunder methods added by attrs, so cmp methods and `__init__` fail.  This will have to be solved with a mypy plugin, which I'll look into next. Same goes for `attr.make_class` though that's likely to be more difficult.\r\n\r\nOne important thing to note: in order to ensure that `y: str = attr.ib()` does not trigger a mypy error, the return type of `attr.ib` is `Any` instead of `_CountingAttr`.   A side effect of this is that it complicates passing the result of `attr.ib` to functions that expect `_CountingAttr` instances.  There are a handful of strategies to solve this:\r\n\r\n1. use `typing.cast`:  ugly and verbose\r\n2. create, or choose an existing, alias for `attr.ib` that will return `_CountingAttr`, to use with functions like `make_class`. \r\n3. add another argument (`make=True`?) whose presence invokes an `@overload` of `attr.ib` that returns `_CountingAttr`\r\n4. slight variation on 2.  create a public alias for `_CountingAttr` and copy the keyword defaults from `attr.ib` to `_CountingAttr.__init__`.  In other words, if you use static type checking and are working with a function that expects `_CountingAttr` instances, use `_CountingAttr()`  directly instead of `attr.ib()`\r\n\r\n~~I favor the 3rd solution.~~  After some consideration I favor 4.\r\n\r\nIf you're interested in accepting this, the next things to figure out are:\r\n- how to make tests for this, and run them on travis\r\n- how best to install the stubs (should they be moved to [python-typeshed](https://github.com/python/typeshed)?)\r\n\r\nLet me know what you think.\r\n\r\n**edit** added option 4.\r\n\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/issues/238/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python-attrs/attrs/issues/238/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"